# DISABLED 2026-08-08 — this handler made iPhone tethering impossible.
#
# The stock version (kept at /root/preaudit-fix/40-usbmuxd.orig) waited 5s after
# ipheth bound and, if carrier was still 0, ran `usbreset iPhone` + restarted
# usbmuxd.  But carrier CANNOT be up that early: ipheth_carrier_set() refuses to
# query the phone until dev->confirmed_pairing is set, and that only happens once
# an RX URB completes.  So the reset always fired, the reset raised a fresh `bind`
# event, and that re-armed the same 5s timer — an endless reset loop that tore the
# interface down every ~5.5s and guaranteed the link could never establish.
#
# Re-enable only if you find an iPhone that genuinely needs the kick, and then
# gate it so it fires at most once per attach.
exit 0
